                                                      EXPERIMENT 3.2 – Palindrome Linked List (LeetCode 234)
                                                      
AIM: To implement an efficient algorithm to determine whether a singly linked list is a palindrome using O(n) time and O(1) extra space.

ALGORITHM:
i) Start the program.
ii) Initialize two pointers, slow and fast, at the head of the linked list.
iii) Move slow one step and fast two steps at a time to find the middle of the linked list.
iv) Reverse the second half of the linked list.
v) Initialize two pointers to compare the first half and the reversed second half.
vi) Compare the values of corresponding nodes.
vii) If any two values are different, return False.
viii) If all corresponding values are equal, return True.
ix) Stop the program.

CODE:
class Solution:
    def isPalindrome(self, head: ListNode | None) -> bool:
        # Find the middle of the linked list
        slow = head
        fast = head

        while fast and fast.next:
            slow = slow.next
            fast = fast.next.next

        # Reverse the second half
        prev = None
        while slow:
            next_node = slow.next
            slow.next = prev
            prev = slow
            slow = next_node

        # Compare both halves
        left = head
        right = prev

        while right:
            if left.val != right.val:
                return False
            left = left.next
            right = right.next

        return True


      
